module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.string_literal_lowers_to_one_class_stamped_atom

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data string_literal_lowers_to_one_class_stamped_atom: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "string_literal_lowers_to_one_class_stamped_atom" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "a string literal lowers to one class-stamped atom: v2 lowers every string literal to the same childless atom, `dag_token_string_literal`. The terminal is class-stamped, so the authored text is not in the tree, and `\"abc\"` and `\"xyz\"` lower to one node. It is the class the caret symbol had before MQ-1 PR-2 (gunbc.recurring_failure_mode caret_symbol_has_no_lowered_form, reference_conservation_population_omits_class_stamped_terminals), for strings.",

    "FOUND 2026-09-30 by neat-ibex-696, probing v2 before adding the kernel host-text String (the successor of #12549). tpb_assemble plus infer on `let y: Int = \"abc\"` showed one childless string-literal atom and an underived literal. Typing the literal as host text does not need its value, so the kernel String change types the literal (v2.extdeps.languages.dag DagCanonicalStringLiteral, v2.std.node host_text_type_node) and leaves the value missing. neat-boar-16 ruled the value fix out of that change and routed it to gentle-koi-724's lane, which owns the same machinery as #12420.",

    "HARM, AND WHERE IT BLOCKS: the declared route from host text to the structural carrier is the literal homomorphism (gunbc.structural_realization_bindings literal_homomorphism_rows, UnicodeScalarSequenceUnfold), and it needs the literal's scalars. Without them, a string literal at a v2.std.text String (FreeMonoid<Char>) position cannot be unfolded, so v2 infer REFUSES it at the annotation rather than admitting it (v2.test.claim.body_let_annotation bla_host_text_literal_at_structural_string_refuses). Any consumer that needs the text itself, such as evaluation, emission or equality between two literals, has nothing to read.",

    "CURRENT RUNG: below the floor for the value (two different literals are one node, silently); refused for the structural crossing. CEILING: structurally impossible, because a string literal lowers to a literal carrying its text. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY: the dag grammar lexeme-stamps the string-literal terminal, and body lowering carries it as the literal's payload with its occurrence, as `dag_symbol_literal_node` carries the caret's name. Then two literals with different text are two nodes, and the unfold row can read the scalars. The literal-at-structural-String refusal row then flips to an unfold control.",

    "CLIMBED BY gunbc#12759 (sleek-owl-120), THE TRIGGER'S CAPABILITY. A string literal now lowers to the string-literal atom with its decoded value as one named payload (`v2.extdeps.languages.dag` `dag_string_literal_node`, `string_literal_value_field`), so two literals with different text are two nodes. #12760's literal arm reads that value (`DagCanonicalStringLiteral { value }` through `dag_string_literal_value_symbol_optional`), and infer types the payload atom as host text by its own family (`InferStringValuePayload`), never as a digit. jolly-boar-246's map-literal key rows, which could not flip on the collapsed atom, flip with #12759 plus #12760 (measured by claim_batch). RESIDUAL, A DIFFERENT OBSTACLE: a string literal at a v2.std.text String (FreeMonoid<Char>) position still REFUSES instead of unfolding, because v2 infer does not peel an alias to its body at a use site, so it cannot recognize that destination as the unfold row's FreeMonoid over Char (`gunbc.structural_realization_bindings` `literal_homomorphism_rows`). That refusal is located and never an admit. Its trigger is v2 infer resolving an annotation's declaration through its alias to the row's destination.",

    "PLACED AT THE ONE JUDGE, NOT YET FIRING, by quick-hawk-799 (gunbc#12809, stacked on #12760, DRAFT). The fact that a string literal crosses to a structural text type by the declared unfold is wired where a produced occurrence meets its declared type once: `v2.std.inhabitance` `declared_type_inhabitance_at` asks std.literal_elaboration elaborate_literal_at over the ONE row set (gunbc.structural_realization_bindings literal_homomorphism_rows) whenever `v2.compiler.infer` `infer_judge_declared_position` supplies a literal crossing (`infer_literal_crossing`: the canonical literal reader, plus the declared reference peeled to its resolved alias body). No second row, no String arm, no per-position copy. EXECUTED 2026-09-30 on BuildBuddy: the reds cannot yet fire on the real route, for two missing capabilities with owners. (1) DECLARED RETURN: the judge is reached, but ResolvedTree resolved_declarations (#12629) covers only the root module, so an imported alias -- and v2.std.text String is always imported -- cannot be peeled; reading symbol_index would key on authored atoms (DESIGN 4 leaf-name agreement). TRIGGER: royal-stag-371's gunbc#12726 PR2, declaration bodies resolved once per ingest in the declaring module's scope (PR3 has infer read that index). (2) CALL ARGUMENT: a call to a declared fn never reaches the judge; its operator is a declaration reference, not an Arrow, so the application is counted FormalsUnresolved first. TRIGGER: gunbc#12506. Both are pinned expecting-red in v2.test.claim.body_let_annotation (..._blocked_on_import_closure_resolution, ..._blocked_on_declared_callee_formals) and flip to the positive claims when their triggers land. Record fields and #12758's map key reach the same judge through smart-newt-725's #12763 and then share trigger (1). The annotated let still asks v2.std.coercion coercion_cast_crossing, so a literal there refuses (bla_host_text_literal_at_structural_string_refuses); its trigger is routing the annotated-let check to infer_judge_declared_position. The verdict is not yet a recorded LiteralElaboration, so emission does not realize the unfold image. RUNG, structural crossing on v2: unchanged -- refused on every position (never a silent admit), with the lawful admit wired and awaiting the two triggers.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.extdeps.languages.dag", decl_name: "dag_canonical_literal_from_node", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.extdeps.languages.dag", decl_name: "dag_string_literal_node", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.body_let_annotation", decl_name: "bla_host_text_literal_at_structural_string_refuses", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.body_let_annotation", decl_name: "bla_string_literal_return_at_structural_string_blocked_on_import_closure_resolution", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.std.inhabitance", decl_name: "declared_type_inhabitance_at", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.infer", decl_name: "infer_literal_crossing", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
